candidates.evidence:
expect(knex({ client: 'oracle' })).to.throw(
      /Knex: run\n$ npm install oracle/
    );

candidates.suggested_fix:
expect(() => knex({ client: 'oracle' })).to.throw(
      /Knex: run\n\$ npm install oracle/
    );

candidates.body:
**Testing (high)**: The assertion will fail to catch the error correctly because the throwing function is executed immediately instead of being passed as a callback, and the regex contains an unescaped '$' character which is treated as an end-of-line anchor.

```
expect(knex({ client: 'oracle' })).to.throw(
      /Knex: run\n$ npm install oracle/
    );
```

**Suggested fix:** expect(() => knex({ client: 'oracle' })).to.throw(
      /Knex: run\n\$ npm install oracle/
    );

